CHECKER: checker-a11y
FAMILY: anthropic
TASK: U12
ATTEMPT: 1
---

METHOD: Live render only. Started `scripts/whatif-verify.sh start 8092`
(throwaway data copy), rendered the REAL running /accounts page with
Playwright + chromium (installed to scratchpad, not vendored), ran
@axe-core/playwright against it in light and `class="dark"` (the exact
mechanism base.html's own theme bootstrap uses — confirmed by reading
layouts/base.html:24-26). Every `<details>`-equivalent disclosure (the
Add-account panel and all per-account Edit panels) was opened via real
button clicks before each axe pass, per U-RUN-SPEC's rendered-bar
contract. Stopped the verify server on :8092 afterward (script's own
teardown). Diff attribution used `git diff HEAD` (this attempt's
uncommitted changes are the only diff on these two files; `git status`
confirmed no other uncommitted files) and `git show master:...` for the
focus-handler comparison.

CHECK 1 — Full axe sweep, both themes, all panels open: PASS
  0 violations in light, 0 violations in dark (axe full ruleset, not just
  color-contrast). Evidence: /tmp/.../a11y-u12/audit-opened.json — both
  `"violations": []`.

CHECK 2 — Disclosures are real buttons, keyboard-operable, ids match:  PASS
  - `[data-toggle-target="accounts-new-form-panel"]` and every
    `[data-toggle-target^="acct-edit-panel-"]` are `<BUTTON>` tags (not
    div-onclick), each carries `aria-expanded`/`aria-controls`, and the
    `aria-controls` value matches the controlled panel's real `id`
    (accounts.html:242-249 add button ↔ #accounts-new-form-panel;
    :375-381 edit button ↔ #acct-edit-panel-{{.ID}}).
  - Tab reaches the Add button and each Edit button (native `<button>`,
    no tabindex override).
  - Enter toggles `aria-expanded` false→true and un-hides the panel;
    Space toggles it back true→false and re-hides it (verified on the
    Add button; same delegated handler drives every Edit button
    identically — accounts.js:23-31).
  - While collapsed, `#acct-new-id` inside the Add panel is NOT
    reachable (`tabIndex >= 0 && offsetParent !== null` is false); once
    opened it becomes focusable and was actually focused via `.focus()`.
  Evidence: /tmp/.../a11y-u12/keyboard.js output — all fields true as
  expected (addBtnTag=BUTTON, editIdsMatch=true, idFieldTabbableWhileHidden
  =false, idFieldReachableAfterOpen=true, editBtnTag=BUTTON, etc).

CHECK 3 — revealAncestorPanel / stranded-error recovery: FAIL (see below)

CHECK 4 — Exactly one <h1>, clean heading order: PASS
  h1 "Accounts" → h2 "Add an account" → h2 "Your accounts" → h3 (per
