=== FAILURE — CHECK 3 detail ===

ACCESSIBILITY.md point 5 / WCAG 2.2 3.3.1 (Error Identification):
web/static/js/accounts.js:225-236 (htmx:afterSwap handler), interacting
with web/templates/pages/accounts.html's disclosure panels added by this
task (accounts.html:242 `#accounts-new-form-panel`, :381
`#acct-edit-panel-{{.ID}}`).

The focus-picking line is:
    var focusable = target.querySelector('[data-focus-target]')
                  || target.querySelector('[aria-invalid="true"]');
This picks the FIRST element in DOCUMENT ORDER carrying a
`data-focus-target` attribute — not the field matching the actual
`ErrorField`. The Add-account form's `id` and `name` inputs
(accounts.html:261 `data-focus-target="id"`, :280
`data-focus-target="name"`) carry that attribute UNCONDITIONALLY
(regardless of ErrorField), and the Add form is the first thing in
document order, before the per-account cards. This selector logic is
byte-identical to master's inline script (`git show
master:web/templates/pages/accounts.html` lines 320-321) — the root
cause is PRE-EXISTING, carried over verbatim by the U7 JS-extraction, not
authored by U12.

Before U12, this mis-selection was harmless-ish: every form was always
visible, so a misdirected focus still landed on an on-screen field while
the real error (marked `aria-invalid="true"`, still visible) sat in
plain sight a scroll away. U12 changed the ground truth by wrapping the
edit forms in `hidden` panels, and its own manifest claims the new
`revealAncestorPanel()` (accounts.js) makes this safe: "a validation
error on a hidden Add/Edit form still gets focus and is visible." That
claim is FALSE for edit-form errors — reproduced live:

  1. Opened the Edit panel for "USAA Checking"
     (`#acct-edit-panel-usaa-checking`).
  2. Cleared its `name` field via the DOM (bypassing the browser's native
     `required` popup with `form.noValidate = true`, exactly reproducing
     what a user who clears a pre-filled name and submits would trigger
     server-side) and submitted.
  3. Server correctly returned `ErrorField="name"`, banner text "account
     name is required" (role="alert", accounts.html:155 — announced to
     AT correctly).
  4. After the htmx swap: `#acct-edit-panel-usaa-checking` is REHIDDEN
     (fresh swap renders every panel closed) and `aria-expanded="false"`
     on its Edit button — i.e. NOT revealed, even though it contains the
     one input server-marked `aria-invalid="true"` for this exact error.
  5. Focus instead landed on `#acct-new-id` (the Add form's unrelated ID
     field, which has no error, no `aria-invalid`), and its ancestor —
     the ADD panel, not the edit panel — is the one `revealAncestorPanel`
     opened.

  Reproduction script/output: /tmp/.../a11y-u12/reveal2.js,
  /tmp/.../a11y-u12/reveal2 output:
    "panelId": "acct-edit-panel-usaa-checking",
    "errorText": "account name is required",
    "panelHiddenAfterError": true,
    "toggleBtnExpandedAfterError": "false",
    "activeElementId": "acct-new-id",
    "activeElementVisible": true

Net effect: a keyboard/AT user editing an account, hitting a real
validation error, is left with focus sitting in the "Add an account" ID
field — an invitation to create a NEW account — while the actual erroring
edit form remains collapsed and undiscoverable except by re-reading the
generic banner text and manually reopening the correct card's Edit
disclosure by trial. That is exactly the "stranded" failure mode task
instruction #3 named and asked me to verify against — and it reproduces
on the FIRST account tried, not an edge case.

Scope attribution: the underlying `querySelector` mis-match is
pre-existing (OBSERVATION, not this FAIL's basis by itself). The FAIL is
that U12 wrapped previously-always-visible forms in `hidden` panels
without correcting (or working around) that pre-existing selector, so
the emergent, task-introduced consequence is a real error becoming
inaccessible by focus. U12's own manifest asserts this exact path was
verified working; it was not (the manifest's probe apparently exercised
only the Add-form's OWN errors, where the bug is inert because Add's `id`
field happens to be both the wrongly-selected target AND inside the
correct panel).

Minimal fix for the worker: match on ErrorField, not "first
data-focus-target in the document" — e.g.
`target.querySelector('[data-focus-target="' + errorField + '"]')`
using a data attribute carrying the server's ErrorField (or scope the
query to `[aria-invalid="true"]` first, which IS correctly conditional
per-field, ahead of the unconditional `data-focus-target` fallback).

=== OBSERVATIONS (not FAILs) ===

- O1 (pre-existing, master-identical): the `data-focus-target="id"` /
  `data-focus-target="name"` attributes on the Add form's `id`/`name`
  inputs are unconditional (present regardless of ErrorField), which is
  what makes the document-order mis-selection possible at all. Present
  verbatim in master; not introduced here.
- O2 (pre-existing): `acct-edit-name-{{.ID}}` has no `aria-describedby`
  linking it to any error text (ACCESSIBILITY.md point 5's other clause),
  same on master — U12 did not touch this field's markup beyond moving
  it into the new hidden wrapper.
- O3: the per-account "add anchor" form (anchor_date/anchor_amount) was
  correctly left OUTSIDE any disclosure by this task (per the manifest's
  stated scope), so its own pre-existing focus/reveal behavior is
  unaffected by U12 either way.
- O4: `make css` produced a byte-identical `tailwind.css` (no new classes
  needed); confirmed via `git status` showing no diff on that file,
  consistent with the manifest's claim.

